>HEAD

  DATAID="INFODATE1"
  ACQBY="AusMT test fixture"
  FILEBY="AusMT test fixture"
  PROSPECT="Create-time precedence fixture"
  LOC="Fixture"
  LAT=-31.500000
  LONG=139.250000
  ELEV=210.00
  ACQDATE=2009-11-02
  FILEDATE=2011-07-18
  UNITS=M
  EMPTY=1.0E+32
  STDVERS=1.0

>INFO   MAXLINES=1000

  MINTED FIXTURE - NOT CUSTODIAN DATA. Identity, geometry and every datum are
  invented; no byte is copied from any custodian or staged file.

  It pins ONE precedence rule the sample EDIs cannot show, because in those
  the two declared dates agree. mt_metadata seeds a station's declared
  creation time from the HEAD FILEDATE and then lets an INFO key overwrite
  it, so a file declaring both resolves to the INFO value. The two here are
  more than seven years apart, so a served CreateTime taken from the wrong
  one is unmistakable.

  provenance.creation_time = 2019-03-04T00:00:00+00:00

>=DEFINEMEAS

  MAXCHAN=5
  MAXRUN=999
  MAXMEAS=99999
  UNITS=M
  REFTYPE=CART
  REFLAT=-31.500000
  REFLONG=139.250000
  REFELEV=210.00

 >HMEAS ID= 1001.001 CHTYPE=HX X =  .000000  Y =  .000000  AZM=   0.0000
